{
  "description": "Budgets for AI APIs (FR-31, SEC-45, T-07). `amounts`: decimal text → micros (millionths) or null. `usage`: the usage an answer (`body`, its exact text) reports in each format → `{input, output}` tokens or null (the gate answers `upstream_usage_invalid`). `charges`: usage and an optional `cost` → `{tokens, micros}`, micros = ⌈(input × inputPerMillion + output × outputPerMillion) in micros / 10^6⌉. `reservations`: what one request reserves, `reserve` tokens priced as input at the higher of the two prices. `sequences`: steps against one budget, starting with nothing spent. `{now, request}`: refused (seconds until the period ends) when the spending — open reservations included — has reached `tokens` or the cost `limit`, else null and the reservation is added → `{refused, spent}`. `{now, answer, result}`: the answer to that earlier request; its reservation is replaced by the charge of `result` (`{input, output}` usage; `uncountable` = the reservation itself; `not_charged` = nothing), unless the period it was made in has ended → `{spent}`. `spent` is `{tokens, micros}` of the period holding `now` (0 once it ended); both are capped at 10^15 tokens and 10^17 micros.",
